{"title":"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Easy_and_simple,_no_need_to_know_the_sides_of_the_triangle!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Easy and simple, no need to know the sides of the triangle!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_DDM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by DDM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Stem_Simplified\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Stem Simplified</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Fast_and_Easy_🔥🚀)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Fast and Easy 🔥🚀)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Thinking_Feet\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Thinking Feet</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Speedrun/Fast_WITH_QUICK_EXPLANATION!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Speedrun/Fast WITH QUICK EXPLANATION!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Haruki has a piece of wire that is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> centimeters long. He wants to bend it to form each of the following shapes, one at a time:\n</p><p>A regular hexagon with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cm.\n</p><p>A square with area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/2/282ee9e561f0f91753c0a47b07d23add9c9f09ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36 \\hspace{3pt} \\text{cm}^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>A right triangle whose legs are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cm long.\n</p><p>Which of the shapes can Haruki make?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/b/07b23e6f21862555ab6d0446bc698311cc2336cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} \\hspace{3pt} \\text{Triangle only} \\\\ \\textbf{(B)} \\hspace{3pt} \\text{Hexagon and square only} \\\\ \\textbf{(C)} \\hspace{3pt} \\text{Hexagon and triangle only} \\\\  \\textbf{(D)} \\hspace{3pt} \\text{Square and triangle only} \\\\ \\textbf{(E)} \\hspace{3pt} \\text{Hexagon, triangle, and square}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"98\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>\tTo solve this problem we can find the perimeter of each of the given spaces and check if it is less than 24.\n</p><p>The first shape is a regular hexagon with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The hexagon has a perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/1/171948e34a4fd62d00a56a97fcd05faf44ff750e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\cdot 5 = 30$\" width=\"73\" height=\"12\" /> centimeters. The second shape is a square with area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> or a side length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Then the perimeter of all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> sides is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> centimeters. Finally, we need to find the perimeter of a right triangle with legs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> centimeters. The hypotenuse of the right triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> so the total perimeter is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/2/b7283211787e10ae4b6c5ee0b823a7e5ac2d5faa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 + 8 + 10 = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"125\" height=\"15\" /> centimeters.\n</p><p>Thus, only the square and the triangle can be made with 24 centimeters of wire so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/5/7656d721a108194609b845c22f98319aba171566.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(D) } \\text{Square and triangle only}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"228\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~ LogicalRhino65\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Easy_and_simple.2C_no_need_to_know_the_sides_of_the_triangle.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Easy_and_simple,_no_need_to_know_the_sides_of_the_triangle!)\">Solution 2 (Easy and simple, no need to know the sides of the triangle!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Easy and simple, no need to know the sides of the triangle!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, consider the regular hexagon. A regular hexagon with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cm has perimeter\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/7/597bb9333e38b77f054207665353089ef3e62289.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6\\cdot 5 = 30$\" width=\"73\" height=\"12\" /> cm, which exceeds the available <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cm of wire. Therefore, the hexagon cannot be formed, eliminating answer choices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/1/b7193f66028e13f331d53ff5e6942c4b05587465.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/9/169b8d69bd74a91e72ec43123070d770633a340a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e41e3cd48cee2c6866cfbb4386a8e99d3482f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Next, consider the square. A square with area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/9/289e936df1f32e061deb86f79f4f2ec1193d6026.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36\\text{ cm}^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" /> has side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/e/00e6f895fd03e6f27877a43fa8bb93cdf808a89b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{36}=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> cm, so its perimeter is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/7/2e704988686df11b10e82a9f919f7c6f83df9bd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\cdot 6 = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"76\" height=\"14\" /> cm. Thus, the square can be formed.\n</p><p>At this point, the only remaining answer choices are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/6/a46f6af01fcf3bb5f6cac2316bc4de9bb3906bec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/0/b305929a95b53f14a0ad53eba1d8560626e1f28b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />. But since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/0/3701b28247f1e9b4ce1824d6f2c952679b2d7f89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) Triangle only}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"148\" height=\"18\" /> does not include the square and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/0/b305929a95b53f14a0ad53eba1d8560626e1f28b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> does, the correct answer must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/0/b305929a95b53f14a0ad53eba1d8560626e1f28b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, the shapes Haruki can make are the square and the triangle, and the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/e/06eac20a9b0d57fc59b1be780c1367c6e6d88b9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) Square and triangle only}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"255\" height=\"30\" />. Conveniently, the triangle is listed last, so the shapes can be evaluated in the given order.\n</p><p>~jeremyq\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/gzXlOkLl24U\">https://youtu.be/gzXlOkLl24U</a>\n</p><p>~TheSmartGreekMathDude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_DDM\">Video Solution by DDM</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by DDM\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/nY1hhVbEeBk\">https://youtu.be/nY1hhVbEeBk</a>\n</p><p>~piggydude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Stem_Simplified\">Video Solution by Stem Simplified</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Stem Simplified\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GJX9bHE7yPI\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GJX9bHE7yPI</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Fast_and_Easy_.F0.9F.94.A5.F0.9F.9A.80.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Fast_and_Easy_🔥🚀)\">Video Solution (Fast and Easy 🔥🚀)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Fast and Easy 🔥🚀)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cBmFo5Gsq28&amp;list=PLpxy89D2tvVpAjkqMVFD_4gKzoEwPoj9l&amp;index=28\">2026 AMC8 #3</a>\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://piacademyus.org/\">By piacademyus.org</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Thinking_Feet\">Video Solution by Thinking Feet</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Thinking Feet\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Dp6yIwyn-N8\">https://youtu.be/Dp6yIwyn-N8</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YJnsl4zjdK8\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YJnsl4zjdK8</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Speedrun.2FFast_WITH_QUICK_EXPLANATION.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Speedrun/Fast_WITH_QUICK_EXPLANATION!)\">Video Solution (Speedrun/Fast WITH QUICK EXPLANATION!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Speedrun/Fast WITH QUICK EXPLANATION!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/YZc76c2qWqE?si=8wwlWtwpnmt8fzDI&amp;t=99\">https://youtu.be/YZc76c2qWqE?si=8wwlWtwpnmt8fzDI&amp;t=99</a>\n</p><p>~sfactorial\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_.28AIME_Qualifier.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3GmtxMC-W1I&amp;t=180s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3GmtxMC-W1I&amp;t=180s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_.28AIME_Qualifier.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\">Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Vid